https://i.discogs.com/k-D9FNcIE43mn0CEKBsotS_1vlYgVewtsHAt_TARzwM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc2OTgt/MTM1Njg2Mzc4MC04/OTA2LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"German Eurodance act created in 1989 by Frankfurt-based producer duo [a48689] and [a48688].\r\nWhen Ancilotti and Münzing aka [a39474] and [a54860] first released an early version of their song \"The Power\" under their alias [a14485], they were facing a bunch of copyright infringements, as the big number of samples, they used on this version were unauthorized.\r\nThey made a second try, now incorporating Pittsburg based US-rapper [a635358] aka [a108652]. The resulting group was calle \"Snap!\" after a sequencer function and imitating the logo of Soul label [l24936]. Additionally to the three involved musicians, the band consisted additionally from numerous vocalists, which changed over the times. While Turbo B. was the face of the band, the vocalists stayed in the backgroud mainly. In chronologic order, some of the featuring vocalists were [a704153], [a39477], [a19619] and [a58266] to name a few.\r\nAfter having a number of chart hits, the band changed its style from Eurohouse and Eurodance to Trance in 1993. As the rap parts disappeared from the songs, Turbo B. did no more have a function within the group and left the band. In 1996, the band went on a 4-year hiatus due to missing success.\r\nIn 2000, the band was reactivated and in 2002, Turbo B. returned to the band. The new era of Snap! was considerably less successful than the beginnings. Many of the released titles were in fact remixes and reworks of old works. \r\nSnap! still exists, but mainly now as group of Penny Ford, rapper Benjamin Lowe aka Stoli and Turbo B.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:7698","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":false,"id":19619,"name":"Thea Austin"},{"active":true,"id":39477,"name":"Penny Ford"},{"active":true,"id":48688,"name":"Luca Anzilotti"},{"active":true,"id":48689,"name":"Michael Münzing"},{"active":false,"id":58266,"name":"Niki Haris"},{"active":false,"id":58953,"name":"Janice Robinson"},{"active":false,"id":198125,"name":"Paula Brown"},{"active":false,"id":382494,"name":"Loc (2)"},{"active":false,"id":635358,"name":"Durron Butler"},{"active":false,"id":704153,"name":"Jackie Harris"},{"active":false,"id":1404221,"name":"Paulette Parker"},{"active":false,"id":2778894,"name":"Sarah Martin (4)"}],"namevariations":["S N A P","S.N.A.P","SNAP","Shap","Sn!p","Snad","Snap","Snap !","Snap!Attack","Snap.","Snape","The Snap","劈啪合唱團","霹靂合唱團"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/7698-Snap!","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.facebook.com/snapofficial","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snap!"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/8020619/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"8020619","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:8020619","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/8020619-DJ-SIMLOCKED","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/8285/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"8285","image":"https://i.discogs.com/dRE3qNK02sfp7kYbrTHvwEtfbjjc7niFzjW95KJbCfs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTgyODUt/MTc5MTYyNzczNy03/OTI1LnBuZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/PIhxVKdvI4HYT5pZr6mzLBxyKs2J8FesSOoVHbezRUw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTgyODUt/MTc5MTYyNzczNy03/OTI1LnBuZw.jpeg","profile":"American singer and songwriter, born 21 August 1979 in Harlem, New York City, USA.\r\n\r\nKelis graduated from Fiorello H. LaGuardia High School in 1997, being a violin player for 14 years, and signed a production deal with the then-under-the-radar production team [url=http://www.discogs.com/artist/17110-Neptunes-The]The Neptunes[/url]. They produced her debut album \"Kaleidoscope\" (1999), released on Virgin. Her sophomore release, \"Wanderland\" (2001), wasn't as fortunate and did not get released in the US, which led to tensions with Virgin; Kelis was later dropped because of lackluster performance. She found solace in a romance with rapper [a=Nasir Jones] whom she married to in 2005 and divorced from in 2010.\r\n\r\nHer career started going full throttle with the buzz surrounding her third album, \"Tasty\" (2003), which features hit single \"Milkshake\" that was nominated for a Grammy for Best Urban/Alternative Performance in 2004 and peaked at #1 on Billboard's Hot Dance/Club Play Songs chart in December 2003 with remixes by X-Press 2 and DJ Zinc.\r\n\r\n\"Kelis Was Here\" (2006) was certified Silver in the UK for sales of over 60,000 copies. Things went quiet for a while, until Kelis returned to the scene with her first electronic album titled \"Flesh Tone\" (2010), which features production by the likes of [a=David Guetta], [a=Benny Benassi] and [a=Boys Noize], amongst others.\r\n\r\nIn April 2014, Kelis released her sixth studio album \"Food\". Fully produced by [a=David Andrew Sitek], the album sees Kelis heading in a new musical direction with the album containing soul, funk and gospel elements.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:8285","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":202726,"name":"Kelis Rogers"},{"id":9688081,"name":"Kelis Jones-Rogers"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":394805,"name":"Alfredo Ortiz"}],"namevariations":["Helis","K.","K3Li5","Kalis","Kayliz","Kelis*","Kellis","Kelys","Kimberly","ケリス","酷莉絲"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/8285-Kelis","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.iamkelis.com","http://soundcloud.com/iamkelis","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelis","http://www.youtube.com/iamkelis","http://www.youtube.com/user/KelisVEVO","http://www.youtube.com/user/OfficialKelis","https://www.instagram.com/kelis?igsh=MXNqeGE0cWN5YzZreg==","https://www.facebook.com/i.am.kelis"]}},"/api/discogs